# =============================================================================
# experiment/contactangle/wedgevanish_T-20_theta120.opts
#
# WEDGE, vapour + thermal reservoirs. The companion to wedge150_*, which is
# sealed; run both to separate what the boundary condition does from what the
# contact angle does.
#
# These match the 2026-08-07 wedge_bc campaign's rhov_eq_eq case. Its staged
# opts were read on 2026-09-19 and carried exactly:
#     -flag_BC_Tfix 1        -flag_BC_rhovfix 1     -rhovfix_axis 0
#     -rhovfix_lo 1.000000   -rhovfix_hi 1.000000   -grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0
#     -humidity 1.00         -temp -20.0            -t_final 7.776e6
# Everything above is reproduced here except t_final, which is 1.3e7 (150 d)
# rather than 7.776e6 (90 d) so this run and its sealed twin share a clock;
# truncate at 90 d to compare against the August campaign directly.
#
# The values are recorded here because that batch is NO LONGER ON DISK -- it was
# under HPC_results/.../batch_2026-08-07__07.26.38_wedge_bc and has since been
# removed, so this header is now the only local record of its BCs.
#
# So the contact angle is the only thing that differs from that campaign, and
# the only driver within these runs.
#
# Expect the angle to come out slightly OFF Young here, and that is the point of
# running the pair. A reservoir keeps the interface exchanging mass, so it never
# reaches steady state; its meniscus carries a Gibbs-Thomson supersaturation and
# a moving interface satisfies sigma = d0*chi + beta*v_n rather than d0*chi
# alone. In the flat channel that cost -1.019 deg at theta=60 against +0.004
# sealed. What the reservoir buys in exchange is NET growth or shrinkage, which
# a sealed box cannot show at all -- vapour there holds ~1e-6 of the water.
#
# LEG 1 of a chain. t_final = 2.6e7 s = 301 days, about 20 h of wall clock --
# the whole run does not fit in one job.
#
# The lens needs of order 1400 days to vanish (see below), which is ~93 h at
# dtmax and more once dt collapses in the endgame. That is four to five 24 h
# jobs, so run it as a chain with -initial_cond and -t_start:
#
#   leg 1:  submit as-is                       t: 0      -> 2.6e7
#   leg n:  -initial_cond <leg n-1 final sol_*.dat> \
#           -t_start <leg n-1 t_final>  -t_final <+2.6e7>
#
# -t_start keeps the clock absolute so the legs stitch into one time series;
# without it each leg restarts at zero and any rate measured across a join is
# wrong. Check the banner says "RESTART: loading solution from ..." -- if that
# line is missing the restart silently did not happen and the leg started from
# the IC instead.
#
# STOP EARLY if plots/phi_bounds.png shows the excursion climbing out of the
# rounding floor, or if distinct sol_*.dat fingerprints stop increasing. Either
# means the lens has stopped being resolvable and later legs measure nothing.
#
# Why the lens vanishes at all:
#
# At theta = 120 the meniscus is convex, so a reservoir held at flat saturation
# is undersaturated for it and the lens loses mass indefinitely -- there is no
# equilibrium to stop at, unlike the sealed case. The 150-day run lost 21.8 %;
# linear extrapolation gives ~690 days, and this allows 2x that because the rate
# is not constant. dV/dt ~ L * v_n falls as the lens shrinks, while the rising
# curvature pushes v_n up, and which wins is exactly what this run measures.
#
# THE POINT IS THE ENDGAME, not the bulk of it. As the lens half-width
# approaches the interface width the two menisci start to overlap, the phase
# field can no longer represent a distinct lens, and the model stops being
# meaningful before the volume reaches zero. eps = 8.584e-7 m against an initial
# thickness of order 1e-4, so the last two decades of shrinkage are where the
# discretisation is under test. Expect dt to collapse as v_n diverges (the
# interface-CFL limiter will clamp on |dphi| per step), and watch
# plots/phi_bounds.png: an excursion outside [0,1] appearing late in the run is
# the signature of the lens becoming unresolvable.
#
# Original 150-day note ~ 6 tau at the wedge-scale channel's tau = 24-34 d. Longer
# than the 90-day runs because the point here is the plateau, not the rate, and
# the flat-90 IC makes the approach cheaper anyway.
# =============================================================================
-t_final 2.6e7

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-beta_sub0 3.9704e6                     # K&P beta0 at -20 C (alpha_c = 2e-3)
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                      # physical capillary length at -20 C

# --- the substrate ---
# gamma_ia = 0.109 (the solver default), gamma_as - gamma_is = 0.0545
#   cos(theta) = -0.0545/0.109 = -0.5000  ->  theta = 120 deg
-gamma_as 0.300
-gamma_is 0.3545000

# --- reservoirs: T on every face, vapour on the x-faces only ---
# Pinning vapour on the y walls would feed ice directly at its contact line and
# corrupt the angle; pinning T there is harmless, regolith being a thermal bath.
-flag_BC_Tfix 1
-flag_BC_rhovfix 1
-rhovfix_axis 0
-rhovfix_lo 1.000000
-rhovfix_hi 1.000000

-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2
-outp 0
-n_out 200
